  "result": "All seven tests pass (the original four plus the three new ones).\n\nWhat changed in `editor/buffer.py`:\n\n- **Generalized the edit record.** Every edit is now stored as \"replace `old` with `new` at `pos`\". Insert has an empty `old`, delete has an empty `new`, and its inverse is just the two strings swapped. This removed the separate insert/delete kinds and made replace a natural single command.\n- **Added `replace(pos, n, s)`.** It records the text it overwrites and the new text in one command, so undo and redo treat it as one step. It uses the same bounds checks as delete.\n- **Added `history_len()`.** Returns the size of the undo stack.\n- **Added `undo_all()`.** Calls undo until it returns False, so every step lands on the redo stack in order.\n- **Factored the bounds check** into a shared helper used by insert, delete, and replace. Behavior is unchanged from before.",
